    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d337">

                <pb facs="0325" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.01/29</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of the
                        American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Duggan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Legal
                        Adviser</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hackworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-05">January 5, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Hackworth</hi>: In the case of the recent change
                    of government in Brazil, before President Vargas term of office expired the
                    Constitution was abrogated and a new Constitution proclaimed which continues him
                    in office subject to a plebiscite at some as yet undetermined date. Inasmuch as
                    the Department may be confronted with similar situations in other countries I
                    would appreciate your comment with regard to the question as to whether or not
                    the need for recognition arises under the above circumstances.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
